<html>
    <body>
        The following updates are available:
        <table style="border: 1px solid;border-collapse=collapse;margin-top: 5px;">
            <tr>
                <th style="border: 1px solid;border-collapse=collapse;">Package Name</th>
                <th style="border: 1px solid;border-collapse=collapse;">Installed Version</th>
                <th style="border: 1px solid;border-collapse=collapse;">Available Version</th>
            </tr>
        {{#each available-updates.data}}
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px solid;border-collapse=collapse;">{{this.package-name}}</td>
                <td style="border: 1px solid;border-collapse=collapse;">{{this.installed-version}}</td>
                <td style="border: 1px solid;border-collapse=collapse;">{{this.available-version}}</td>
            </tr>
        {{/each}}
        </table>

        <h3>What to do</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Update joseph. From the Mac:
<pre>ssh root@joseph.tailf69bc5.ts.net
apt update &amp;&amp; apt dist-upgrade</pre></li>
            <li>If the list above has a <code>proxmox-kernel</code> package, reboot so the new
                kernel is used. Every guest restarts with it:
<pre>reboot</pre>
                Give hermit a few minutes to come back up.</li>
            <li>After a reboot, unseal Vault. From the Mac:
<pre>cd ~/mediasafe-gitops
export BW_SESSION="$(bw unlock --raw)"
export KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/homelab.yaml
bootstrap/vault-unseal</pre>
                It prints "Unsealed." when done. If it says it could not read Vault's status,
                Vault isn't up yet: wait a minute and run the last line again.</li>
        </ol>
    </body>
</html>
